        <title>Get started with the AWS Local Zone in Istanbul</title>
        <published>2026-11-28T07:50:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2026-11-28T08:10:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>Unknown</name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="/technology/aws-local-zone-istanbul/"/>
        <id>/technology/aws-local-zone-istanbul/</id>
        
        <content type="html" xml:base="/technology/aws-local-zone-istanbul/">&lt;p&gt;AWS Local Zones bring compute, storage, and networking closer to end users for single-digit millisecond latency. The &lt;strong&gt;Istanbul Local Zone&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;, Zone ID &lt;code&gt;euc1-ist1-az1&lt;/code&gt;) extends the &lt;strong&gt;Europe (Frankfurt)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1&lt;/code&gt;) parent region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This walkthrough covers the full end-to-end flow in the AWS Management Console (click any screenshot to zoom in):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opting in to the Istanbul Local Zone via AWS Global Views&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating a VPC with &lt;strong&gt;one&lt;/strong&gt; subnet in &lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launching a &lt;strong&gt;Debian&lt;/strong&gt; EC2 virtual machine (&lt;code&gt;c7i.large&lt;/code&gt;) in that Local Zone subnet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;1-opt-in-to-the-istanbul-local-zone&quot;&gt;1. Opt in to the Istanbul Local Zone&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you can create subnets or launch instances in a Local Zone, your AWS account must opt in to the zone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch your AWS Console region to &lt;strong&gt;Europe (Frankfurt)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open the &lt;strong&gt;EC2 Console&lt;/strong&gt; and navigate to &lt;strong&gt;Settings&lt;/strong&gt; → &lt;strong&gt;Zones&lt;/strong&gt;. AWS now manages Local Zone opt-ins in &lt;strong&gt;AWS Global Views&lt;/strong&gt;—click &lt;strong&gt;Open Global Views&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/01-ec2-settings-zones.png&quot; alt=&quot;EC2 Settings Zones tab showing the Open Global Views button&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In &lt;strong&gt;AWS Global View → Regions and Zones&lt;/strong&gt;, switch to the &lt;strong&gt;Local Zones&lt;/strong&gt; tab and locate &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Turkey (Istanbul)&lt;/code&gt;, Parent Region &lt;code&gt;Europe (Frankfurt)&lt;/code&gt;, Zone ID &lt;code&gt;euc1-ist1-az1&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select the radio button next to &lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt; and click &lt;strong&gt;Opt-in&lt;/strong&gt; (if its status is &lt;code&gt;Not opted in&lt;/code&gt;). Once enabled, the status updates to &lt;strong&gt;Opted in&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/02-local-zones-istanbul.png&quot; alt=&quot;AWS Global View Local Zones tab showing eu-central-1-ist-1a Opted in&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;2-create-a-vpc-with-one-istanbul-local-zone-subnet&quot;&gt;2. Create a VPC with one Istanbul Local Zone subnet&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Next, create a VPC in &lt;code&gt;eu-central-1&lt;/code&gt; with a single public subnet placed in &lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open the &lt;strong&gt;VPC Console&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1&lt;/code&gt;) and click &lt;strong&gt;Create VPC&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Choose &lt;strong&gt;VPC and more&lt;/strong&gt;, set a name prefix (for example &lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz&lt;/code&gt;), and keep the IPv4 CIDR block (&lt;code&gt;10.0.0.0/16&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/03-create-vpc-wizard.png&quot; alt=&quot;Create VPC wizard with VPC and more selected&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under &lt;strong&gt;Number of Availability Zones (AZs)&lt;/strong&gt;, select &lt;strong&gt;1&lt;/strong&gt;. Expand &lt;strong&gt;Customize AZs&lt;/strong&gt;, open the &lt;strong&gt;First availability zone&lt;/strong&gt; dropdown, and select &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;euc1-ist1-az1 (eu-central-1-ist-1a)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. Set &lt;strong&gt;Number of public subnets&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;1&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Number of private subnets&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;0&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;NAT gateways&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;None&lt;/strong&gt;, then click &lt;strong&gt;Create VPC&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/04-create-vpc-az-dropdown.png&quot; alt=&quot;Create VPC wizard selecting 1 AZ and choosing eu-central-1-ist-1a from the dropdown&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you are adding a Local Zone subnet to an existing VPC (via &lt;strong&gt;VPC → Subnets → Create subnet&lt;/strong&gt;), select your VPC (&lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-vpc&lt;/code&gt;), enter a subnet name (&lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-subnet-public-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;), open the &lt;strong&gt;Availability Zone&lt;/strong&gt; dropdown, and choose &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Turkey (Istanbul) / euc1-ist1-az1 (eu-central-1-ist-1a)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with CIDR &lt;code&gt;10.0.16.0/20&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/05-create-subnet-az-dropdown.png&quot; alt=&quot;Create subnet Availability Zone dropdown showing Turkey (Istanbul) / eu-central-1-ist-1a&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Create subnet&lt;/strong&gt; and verify the subnet details: &lt;strong&gt;Availability Zone&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;code&gt;euc1-ist1-az1 (eu-central-1-ist-1a)&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Network border group&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;State&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;Available&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/06-subnet-created.png&quot; alt=&quot;Subnet details confirming eu-central-1-ist-1a and Available state&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;3-launch-a-debian-ec2-vm-in-the-istanbul-local-zone&quot;&gt;3. Launch a Debian EC2 VM in the Istanbul Local Zone&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now launch a Debian EC2 instance inside the Istanbul Local Zone subnet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open &lt;strong&gt;EC2 → Instances → Launch an instance&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enter a name (for example &lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-vm&lt;/code&gt;) and select &lt;strong&gt;Debian&lt;/strong&gt; under &lt;strong&gt;Application and OS Images (Quick Start)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Debian 13 (HVM), SSD Volume Type&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/07-launch-instance-debian.png&quot; alt=&quot;Launch an instance with Debian selected&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under &lt;strong&gt;Instance type&lt;/strong&gt;, choose an instance family supported in the Istanbul Local Zone—such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;c7i.large&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (2 vCPU, 4 GiB memory)—and select your &lt;strong&gt;Key pair (login)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/08-launch-instance-type-keypair.png&quot; alt=&quot;Instance type c7i.large and key pair selection&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand &lt;strong&gt;Network settings → Edit&lt;/strong&gt; and configure:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VPC&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-vpc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subnet&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-subnet-public-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;eu-central-1-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Auto-assign public IP&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;Enable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firewall (security groups)&lt;/strong&gt;: Allow SSH (port 22) as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/09-launch-instance-network.png&quot; alt=&quot;Network settings configured with istanbul-lz-vpc and Istanbul Local Zone subnet&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Launch instance&lt;/strong&gt;, then open the instance summary page. Confirm &lt;strong&gt;Instance state&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;Running&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Instance type&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;c7i.large&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Subnet ID&lt;/strong&gt; points to &lt;code&gt;istanbul-lz-subnet-public-ist-1a&lt;/code&gt;. When connecting over SSH to a Debian AMI, use the default username &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;admin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ssh admin@&amp;lt;public-ip&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/10-instance-running.png&quot; alt=&quot;Running EC2 instance summary in Istanbul Local Zone&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;4-walkthrough-video&quot;&gt;4. Walkthrough video&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;video controls preload=&quot;metadata&quot; style=&quot;width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;&quot; poster=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/10-instance-running.png&quot;&gt;
  &lt;source src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/walkthrough.mp4&quot; type=&quot;video/mp4&quot;&gt;
  &lt;track kind=&quot;subtitles&quot; srclang=&quot;en&quot; label=&quot;English&quot; src=&quot;/media/aws-local-zone-istanbul/walkthrough.vtt&quot;&gt;
&lt;/video&gt;
</content>
        
